{
 "id": 181065,
 "name": "High Assurance Profile for W3C VCDM 2.0 Community Group",
 "is_closed": false,
 "creation-date": "2026-11-12",
 "description": "<p>Increasingly, regulations require verifiable credentials for high-assurance use cases. For example, the EU Artificial Intelligence Act requires data governance and record-keeping for high-risk systems (Art. 10 and 12), and the EU Machinery Regulation covers self-learning safety functions. The <a href=\"https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-model-2.0/\">W3C Verifiable Credentials Data Model (VCDM)</a> can express linked, open-world evidence, but a verifier can rely on it only if contexts are pinned, securing mechanisms are fixed, and status is checkable.</p>\n\n<p>The mission of this group is to develop a High Assurance Profile (HAIP) for the W3C Verifiable Credentials Data Model (VCDM) to create a verifiable evidence layer that agents, industrial AI, and robots can trust, anchored in the eIDAS trust framework (and similar frameworks).</p>",
 "shortname": "vc-haip",
